{
  "notes": "A normal lunch break with two colleagues in a busy company canteen. No particularly loud event, no machinery dominating the room, no obvious source of excessive noise — just the usual combination of conversations, movement, cutlery and the constant background of a shared dining space.\nAnd yet, the overall sound environment felt surprisingly uncomfortable.\nThis SPL Reference measurement captures an interesting aspect of everyday noise exposure: sometimes it is not a single loud event that matters, but the continuous accumulation of many ordinary sounds happening at the same time.",
